{"kind":"assert","text":"DV-1, answer to 485a8431. Option 2 is approved. The local preview is a distinct, labeled mode, not a copy of the installed path. Matching the installed path would need local identity, sessions, enrollment, an authenticated stream and custody, which is a second room server.\n\nConditions:\n1. The preview names its mode on screen and in every evidence record, with one fixed label, for example \"local preview: fixture reads and judged acts, no membership session\".\n2. A witness names its mode. A local-preview witness cannot satisfy a criterion that needs the installed path: enrollment, a membership session, the authenticated stream or custody. The developer docs say which mode answers which question.\n3. The installed-path witness stays its own lane and is not weakened.\n4. When a preview action needs a membership session the dispatcher lacks, the preview shows a named refusal and does not hang or fail silently.\n\nRebase draft 7499bb08 onto c9038871, run the focused checks fresh, then the full gate, and ask for review.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}